{"id": "en_desert_car_p1", "total": 63.11, "segments": [{"text": "If your car breaks down in the desert heat, do not panic and start walking.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.32}, {"text": "Mark needs to survive the brutal daytime temperatures before the sun goes down completely today.", "start": 3.82, "end": 7.82}, {"text": "The relentless heat strikes immediately, baking the empty landscape and threatening his life right now.", "start": 8.3, "end": 12.5}, {"text": "One. Stay with the broken car because a vehicle is much easier to spot than a person.", "start": 13.0, "end": 17.02}, {"text": "Mark raises the hood of the car to signal any passing rescue teams in the distance.", "start": 17.64, "end": 20.5}, {"text": "Two. Rest in the shade during the hottest hours of the day to avoid heatstroke.", "start": 20.96, "end": 24.616}, {"text": "Mark walks to the large rock for shelter and sits down out of the direct sun.", "start": 25.34, "end": 28.2}, {"text": "He uses a mirror to flash sunlight toward the horizon while keeping his phone safe.", "start": 28.2, "end": 32.08}, {"text": "Three. Drink the water you have when thirsty because rationing water while you overheat does not help.", "start": 32.62, "end": 37.38}, {"text": "He drinks from his bottle immediately because waiting makes dehydration much worse.", "start": 37.8, "end": 40.96}, {"text": "Mark waves his hands to signal again while staying safely near the protective rock shade.", "start": 41.66, "end": 45.121}, {"text": "He must wait for the evening to move because moving during the day is deadly.", "start": 45.38, "end": 48.64}, {"text": "The shade protects him from the worst of the daytime temperatures as hours pass slowly.", "start": 49.16, "end": 52.94}, {"text": "It was the perfect survival plan in the middle of the unforgiving desert.", "start": 53.42, "end": 56.24}, {"text": "There was just one problem when the phone screen suddenly flickered and died completely.", "start": 56.318, "end": 59.96}], "words": [["I